    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nA create-owner request is now rejected with **400** when its email domain is on the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n- **`RejectDisposableEmailDomain.java`** \u2014 a `Reject<E>` step that reads the (already normalized/lower-cased) email from the `OwnerFieldsDto` variable, extracts the domain, and throws `DisposableEmailDomainException` when it's blocked. Email is optional, so absent/blank is left untouched.\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainException.java`** \u2014 a checked exception (400).\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java`** + **escalation YAML** \u2014 the global handler that responds `400` with an `errors` body, mirroring the existing `InvalidEmailException` handling.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `rejectDisposableEmail` step immediately after `normalizeEmail` (so syntax is validated and the value lower-cased first) and before `rejectDuplicate`, keeping it under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\nThe domain is matched case-insensitively, and since it runs after `NormalizeEmail`, a syntactically invalid email still returns 400 via the existing rule before the blocklist check.",
